You could reduce the number of junk artifact weapons by making them
less junky--make, say, Giantslayer grant strength to the bearer.  We've
had this thread before, and it's quite interesting.  For other weapons
to be alternatives, they need to either (1) be _much_ better than
grayswandir/brands/etc in a situation that is really somewhat dangerous
(perhaps a Lichbane or a Helm of No Mind Flaying would be used, or if
Demonbane did x4 damage to demons then it would actually be more useful
against Demons than the alternativel) or (2) be generally useful in a
fairly wide array of scenarios so that something besides sheer damage
makes them not a subset of the heavy-hitters (things unrelated to
damage are important here--say the ranged potential of a polearm or
lance, or curse-absorption, light, searching, etc).

Or one could have some of the lesser artifacts show up earlier in the
game--if Valks got Giantslayer as their first sacrifice or somehow else
got it before the quest, then there'd be cause to use it for a while
until they could get Mjollnir/Grayswandir/banes.

