There's no point in having 13 classes that are the same, though.  As it
is, barbarian/caveman/valkyrie/samurai are quite similar.  Wizard,
monk, and ranger are well-differentiated in the mid-late game.  The
others have some differentiation (knights especially), but it'd make
the game more interesting if they had more.

There's nothing wrong with players not playing, say, monks if they
don't enjoy them.  But having CombatWombat1, CombatWombat2, and
CombatWombat3 as classes doesn't really make a lot of sense.

